Subject: [PATCH] builder: support Shelly/RLPM package archives without libalpm

Add an opt-in shelly backend using the existing libarchive dependency. Read
.PKGINFO and the payload inventory directly from package archives, preserving
builder dependency matching, source package names, licensing and version order.
The normal builder extraction path supplies application metadata to its plugins.
No package-manager process or host package database is involved.

Enable with -Dshelly=true -Dalpm=false. Shelly and ALPM are mutually exclusive.
The AppStream library and appstream-util keep their existing APIs. This does not
change Shelly's own AppStream catalog reader or add package transactions.

Tests cover tar/zstd/xz/gzip/bzip2, filename dispatch, filtered extraction,
metadata reload, repeated metadata, invalid/truncated archives, unsafe paths,
metadata bounds and epoch/version/release ordering. Epochs beyond guint are
rejected explicitly because AsbPackage cannot represent them.

